{"version":2,"text":"6.\n\nThe purpose of this email is to\n\nA\n\nreport on a rise in post-surgical complications.\n\nB\n\nexplain the background to a change in patient care.\n\nC\n\nremind staff about procedures for administrating drugs.\n\nE\nL\n\nTo: All staff\n\nSubject: Advisory Email: Safe use of opioids\n\nIn August, an alert was issued on the safe use of opioids in hospitals. This reported the incidence\n\nP\nM\n\nof respiratory depression among post-surgical patients to an average 0.5% – thus for every 5,000\n\nsurgical patients, 25 will experience respiratory depression. Failure to recognise respiratory depression\n\nand institute timely intervention can lead to cardiopulmonary arrest, resulting in brain injury or\n\ndeath. A retrospective multi-centre study of 14,720 cardiopulmonary arrest cases showed that\n\nA\nS\n\n44% were respiratory related and more than 35% occurred on the general care floor. It is therefore\n\nrecommended that post-operative patients now have continuous monitoring, instead of spot checks, of\n\nboth oxygenation and ventilation.\n\nSAMPLE\n\n[CANDIDATE NO.] READING QUESTION PAPER PARTS B & C 07/16\n\nPage 93","layout":{"version":1,"width":595.276001,"height":841.890015,"blocks":[{"text":"6.","lines":[{"text":"6.","x":0.10195758252985576,"y":0.08884928276527902,"width":0.014010307800061994,"height":0.016557982339296437,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"6.","x":0.10195758252985576,"width":0.014010307800061994,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"The purpose of this email is to","lines":[{"text":"The purpose of this email is to","x":0.1495766633467893,"y":0.08899181919861587,"width":0.2240809301499121,"height":0.015809666064278007,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"The","x":0.1495766633467893,"width":0.028944556761998527,"confidence":1},{"text":"purpose","x":0.1831913227088085,"width":0.060694534870052656,"confidence":1},{"text":"of","x":0.2485559601788818,"width":0.014010307800061982,"confidence":1},{"text":"this","x":0.26723637057896443,"widt